# `scripts` was excluded here. Dockerfile.migrate copies it, because
# enroll-production-migrations.cjs and production-migration-preflight.cjs are
# the production path for adopting the migration history, and an excluded
# directory fails silently: the image builds, and the script is simply absent
# at runtime. That is the same defect `public/` carried for the entire life of
# the Azure stack, which is why a test in src/test/bundle-chunk-graph.test.ts
# now guards both. The whole directory is 248K across 24 text files, so keeping
# it in the context costs nothing measurable and a clever negation pattern
# would reintroduce exactly the silence this comment exists to prevent.
